.TH SMTP2 2
.SH NAME
smtp2 \- SMTP message submission over TLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "sys.m";
include "keyring.m";
include "tls12.m";
include "smtp2.m";
smtp2 := load Smtp2 Smtp2->PATH;
Sender: import smtp2;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Smtp2
submits mail through an SMTP server over
.IR tls12 (2),
this tree's verifying TLS 1.2 client \(em never a host command.
It is enough to send through Gmail
.RB ( smtp.gmail.com :465,
implicit TLS).
It is distinct from the plaintext
.IR smtp (2)
module.
.PP
.B init
loads and initialises
.IR tls12 (2)
and a base64 encoder; call it once.
.B connect
dials
.I dialip
(or
.I host
if empty) at
.IR port ,
runs the TLS handshake naming
.I host
for certificate verification, and reads the greeting \(em see
.IR imap4 (2)
for why
.I dialip
is separate.
.PP
The returned
.B Sender
offers, each returning a trailing error string that is nil on success:
.TP
.B ehlo
Send
.B EHLO
and return the server's capability text (its
.B AUTH
line lists the mechanisms).
.TP
.B auth
Authenticate with
.B "AUTH PLAIN"
using
.I user
and
.I pass
(an app password over TLS).
.TP
.B authxoauth2
Authenticate with
.B "AUTH XOAUTH2"
using
.I user
and a caller-supplied OAuth 2.0 bearer
.IR token .
.TP
.B mail
Run a full
.B "MAIL FROM"
/
.B "RCPT TO"
/
.B DATA
transaction; the message is CRLF-normalised and dot-stuffed.
.TP
.B quit
Send
.B QUIT
and close the session.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/smtp2.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upas-send (1),
.IR tls12 (2),
.IR imap4 (2)
.SH BUGS
Only implicit TLS (no STARTTLS).
Authentication is
.B "AUTH PLAIN"
or
.B "AUTH XOAUTH2"
(the caller obtains the OAuth token out of band).
